  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows the permission matrix Allowed set to be empty or contain incorrect mappings. The LeastPrivilege assertion checks that the required role-operation pairs exist; without the fact, these pairs may be missing or incorrect.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_002_CustomerOperations, FR_004_ComplianceReviewerReadOnly
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_002_CustomerOperations: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_004_ComplianceReviewerReadOnly: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows applications to transition between statuses without corresponding audit entries. The AuditCompleteness assertion checks that every status change produces exactly one audit entry; without the fact, transitions could occur without audit records.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, AttributionCorrectness
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - AttributionCorrectness: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_OneInFlightPerCustomer  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_OneInFlightPerCustomer.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a customer to have multiple applications simultaneously in Submitted or Under Review status. The FR_008 assertion checks that at most one in-flight application exists per customer; without the fact, multiple in-flight applications would be permitted.
    expected to FAIL: FR_008_OneInFlightPerCustomer
      - FR_008_OneInFlightPerCustomer: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AssignmentConsistency  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AssignmentConsistency.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows applications at Under Review, Approved, or Rejected status to have no assigned officer or an officer with wrong role. The FR_012 assertion checks that applications in decision-phase statuses have exactly one assigned loan officer; without the fact, this invariant is violated.
    expected to FAIL: FR_012_AssignmentConsistency
      - FR_012_AssignmentConsistency: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OnlyAssignedOfficerDecides  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_OnlyAssignedOfficerDecides.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows decisions to be recorded by any user, not just the assigned loan officer. The FR_013 assertion checks that every decision's recorded actor is the application's assigned officer; without the fact, any user could record a decision.
    expected to FAIL: FR_013_OnlyAssignedOfficerDecides
      - FR_013_OnlyAssignedOfficerDecides: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ComplianceReviewerReadOnly  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_ComplianceReviewerReadOnly.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows the compliance reviewer role to be granted write operations (submit, claim, decide). The FR_004 assertion checks that compliance reviewers have no write permissions; without the fact, write permissions could be incorrectly granted to the compliance role.
    expected to FAIL: FR_004_ComplianceReviewerReadOnly
      - FR_004_ComplianceReviewerReadOnly: PASS (vacuous?)

